Claude's conclusion:
Confirmed directly from the live device: the final state shows `assignedAdapters:{...name:"ethernet1"...}` (the passthrough NIC) correctly attached while `network:{devName:"vif0"...}` only ever carries the single virtual VIF — exactly matching the `len:1` vs expected `2` failure.

**Root cause:** This is the identical, already-confirmed missing-backport bug documented for `TestNetworkAdapterPassthrough` earlier in this same run (and extensively in `live-ledger.md`): `pkg/pillar/cmd/zedagent/handlemetrics.go` builds `ZInfoApp.Network` only from the app's virtual VIF list (`aiStatus.GetAppInterfaceList()`) and never merges `IoAdapterList`/passthrough adapters into it, so a directly-assigned NIC shows under `assignedAdapters` but never under `network`. The fix is commit `979ea453c` ("zedagent: report passthrough NICs in app info and metrics") on master; `git merge-base --is-ancestor 979ea453c HEAD` confirms it's still absent from `17.0-stable` (current HEAD `ef4e3b063`), and `orderedAppNetworkEntries` (the helper the fix adds) is not present in `handlemetrics.go` on this branch. This is the exact `len:1→2` signature that the ledger shows recurring on essentially every nightly run since 2026-11-17, so it's a known, long-standing, unfixed backport gap shared with the earlier `TestNetworkAdapterPassthrough` failure in this run — not a new regression or infra flake.

